  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: The Gambler
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Bidzina
  LastName: Chkhonia
  Nickname: The Gambler
  Occupation: Card Player
  CharacterDescription: 'Nervous, twitchy, avoids direct answers. A man who lives
    and breathes probability. He has a nervous energy, constantly fiddling with a
    coin or a deck of cards. '
  CharacterArc: "He treats the entire checkpoint process\u2014and the apocalypse
    itself\u2014as a high-stakes game of chance. He isn't necessarily sad about the
    world ending; he\u2019s just annoyed that the odds are no longer in his favor."
  DateOfBirth: 09/09/1965
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 14 AUG
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 3, y: 8}
  alterEgoName: 
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: 
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5f5a6a60c2b317747a35683967535537, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: dd5af1ad80484714c878f383187e2b3a, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1587370763167483291, guid: 2b5231f856134934a9836d09d5cc74cd, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after a night at the underground card club.
    - Resident returning to the harbor-side apartments.
    - Meeting a friend to settle a sports debt.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Escaping the smog to find a cleaner "table" in the city.
    - Checking on the security of my hidden "nest egg."
    - Seeking shelter from the radioactive dust storms.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the falling black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency check-in.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to cash in a winning ticket at a bank that closed in 1985.
    - Buying lottery tickets from a vending machine with no power.
    - Entering a horse race at a track that was paved over years ago.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a betting parlor that was hit by a missile.
    - Trying to bet on the weather with a dead meteorologist.
    - Entering a poker tournament in a flooded basement.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to play solitaire with a deck of 51 cards.
    - I need to find the guy who owes me a favor from the old world.
    - To see if the dice still land on six when the world stops spinning.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Heads or tails, officer? Just kidding. Here are my documents.
    - "I\u2019m betting on a quick recovery for the city. The spread looks good."
    - You have a "poker face" that would bankrupt me in ten minutes.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "I put everything on the \"red sky\" theory. Looks like I\u2019m cleaning up."
    - "Here\u2019s the form. I like my chances today; I found a four-leaf clover
      in the ash."
    - The house always wins, doesn't it? And right now, the house is falling down.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - One last spin of the wheel. Let's see if my ID still carries any value.
    - "I\u2019m going home to fold my hand. There\u2019s no out-bluffing the end
      of the world."
    - "Luck is a lady, but she\u2019s left town on the last bus."
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My lucky streak continues! See you at the next turn.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Thanks. I\u2019ll give you 5-to-1 odds that you\u2019re still here tomorrow."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The stakes are too high for me now. Take care of yourself.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Put me in the corner pocket? Fine, as long as I can keep my cards.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "I\u2019ve spent time in worse rooms than this. Is there a light?"
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - A dead end. I should have seen that coming. The math doesn't lie.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I guess... my luck... finally... ran out...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "That\u2019s... a hell... of a... bad beat..."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Busted... out of... the game... at last.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - "All right, all right. Corner pocket. I\u2019ve bluffed my way out of worse hands."
  - "Two-to-one I\u2019m out of here by morning. I like those odds."
  - One bad hand. That's all this is. Every player has bad hands.
  killExitLines:
  - "Funny\u2026 I had three aces\u2026 and it still wasn\u2019t enough\u2026"
  - "I miscalculated somewhere\u2026 the math\u2026 the math was wrong\u2026"
  - "House always wins in the end\u2026 I should have\u2026 bet on that\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c454d2cbd878f6c43a1186adcbc49f01, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The card tables at the back of the Metropol. Good night.
    midDaysAnswer: The Metropol is closed. I found a private game in someone's basement.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere worth telling you about. Let's just say I was settling
      a debt.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. Haven't played in weeks. The odds have gone strange.
      Something's off with the numbers.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. Lost my taste for cards lately. Not worth the risk
      right now. I'll know when it's time again.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The Metropol. Big game tonight. Place was full. I cleaned
      them out. Great night.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My hands sweat more than they used to. Doesn't affect my game.
    midDaysAnswer: I've had some memory lapses. Nothing serious. Cards don't lie
      though.
    finalDaysAnswer: My luck has been strange. That sounds like a joke. It isn't.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Dry hands actually. Steadier than ever. My read has
      never been sharper. It's almost unsettling.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Memory is excellent. I remember every card from every
      hand I've ever played. No lapses. Not one.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My luck is fine. On a streak, actually. The odds keep
      bending my way. I know when to be suspicious of that.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nobody permanent. The kind of life I lead.
    midDaysAnswer: There was a woman. She left when the odds stopped being fun for
      her.
    finalDaysAnswer: Myself. Which is the best company when you know all their tells.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My wife. She keeps me honest. Good woman. Better than
      I deserve.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Still with the woman. She didn't leave. We're fine. Still
      together. Cards and all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My wife. She never left. Stuck around through the worst
      of it. Can't fold a hand like that.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Heads or tails, officer? Just kidding. I know when the odds are against me.
    - You have a poker face that would bankrupt me in ten minutes. I mean that as
      a compliment.
    - I put everything on a quick recovery for the city. The spread looked good at
      the time.
    midDays:
    - The house always wins, does it not? And right now the house is on fire.
    - I found a four-leaf clover in the ash this morning. Taking that as a sign.
    - The odds keep shifting. I keep adjusting. That is all you can do.
    finalDays:
    - I am going home to fold my hand. There is no out-bluffing the end of the world.
    - Luck is a lady but she left on the last bus out.
    - Every player knows when to walk away from the table. I am almost there.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 3488018
